property: data variables type <ME:0000293> = Chemical Measurement <DA:0000005>
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Soil test report of the University of Georgia Soil, Plant, and Water Laboratory (Athens, GA) for Sindhu Jagadamma, completed 2015-08-06; eight depth intervals of the FWB-306 core collected 2015-06-10, each analysed in duplicate
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Lime buffer capacity and pH per the laboratory's methods (UGA CAES publications 7335 and 7336). Equivalent water pH is the laboratory's conversion of the CaCl2 pH (CaCl2 pH + 0.6). Cation exchange capacity is the laboratory's calculated value. Base saturation (extractable bases as a share of cation exchange capacity) is not stored
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Water-extractable organic carbon: 5 g soil shaken in 20 mL deionized water for 15 minutes, mg per kg of soil. Total carbon, total organic carbon and total nitrogen are percent of the soil
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Source: ENIGMA Google Drive, FRC Well Metadata/Core samples/FW306_Sediment_chemical analysis.xls. The ORNL FRC sample collection log carries a rounded copy of these values
